# The SPA fallback, and nothing else: every view in the app is a real path
# (/favorites, /images, /tags/<id>, …) matched by the router in the browser, so
# a hard refresh on one must be served index.html with a 200 rather than a 404.
#
# There is deliberately no proxy rule here any more. Media used to be addressed
# origin-relative, which made this file (and its equivalent on whatever host
# you deploy to) responsible for routing /api/media/* to the API; a host that
# cannot proxy, like the `serve` in this app's own start script, then answered
# every picture with index.html and a 200. Pictures now address the API
# directly, so there is nothing left to forget. See src/lib/media.ts.

